                <p style="margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 0.9rem;">
                    Add resistors to see how they sum up. The total resistance is simply the sum of all parts.
                </p>

                <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 15px;">
                    <button class="btn btn-primary" style="background: #10b981;" onclick="addResistor()">+ Add Resistor</button>
                    <button class="btn btn-outline" style="color: #ef4444; border-color: #ef4444;" onclick="removeResistor()">- Remove</button>
                </div>

                <div id="lab-visuals" style="display: flex; align-items: flex-end; height: 100px; gap: 4px; padding-bottom: 5px; border-bottom: 2px solid #94a3b8;">
                    <!-- Dynamic bars inserted here -->
                </div>

                <div style="margin-top: 10px; font-family: monospace;">
                    <strong>Calculation:</strong> <span id="lab-calc-string">10 + 20 + 30</span> = <span id="lab-total">60</span> Ω
                </div>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- CHARACTERISTICS TABLE -->
        <article class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <div class="card-title">
                    <span class="card-icon">📊</span>
                    Key Characteristics
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="overflow-x: auto;">
                <table>
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Parameter</th>
                            <th>Behavior in Series</th>
                            <th>Explanation</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Current (I)</strong></td>
                            <td style="color: var(--primary);">Constant</td>
                            <td>Same current flows through all components.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Voltage (V)</strong></td>
                            <td style="color: var(--primary);">Divides</td>
                            <td>Total voltage is the sum of individual drops.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Resistance (R)</strong></td>
                            <td style="color: var(--primary);">Increases</td>
                            <td>R<sub>eq</sub> is greater than the largest individual resistor.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </article>

        <!-- SUMMARY CARD -->
        <article class="card">
            <div class="card-header">
                <div class="card-title">
                    <span class="card-icon">📌</span>
                    Important Notes
                </div>
            </div>
            <ul style="padding-left: 20px; color: var(--text-main);">
                <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">If one resistor burns out (open circuit), the entire circuit stops working.</li>
                <li style="margin-bottom: 8px;">Series circuits are not commonly used for household wiring due to this single-point failure risk.</li>
                <li>Used in devices where specific voltage division is required (e.g., potentiometers).</li>
            </ul>
        </article>
